  "tagline": "FAL Labs' C++ DBM library with hash and B+tree files; superseded by its author's Tkrzw.",
  "description": "Kyoto Cabinet is the C++ successor to Tokyo Cabinet, written by Mikio Hirabayashi at FAL Labs: a family of DBM-style databases (file hash, file B+tree, directory and in-memory variants) with thread-safe access, transactions and very fast single-node throughput. Together with the Kyoto Tycoon network server it was a popular lightweight store around 2010. It now receives only occasional build fixes (1.2.80 in 2023), and the author's own pages recommend Tkrzw, his modern replacement. Use it only to keep existing software running.",
